## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

**10 tests, 9 findings: 6 Critical, 3 Medium**

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called, achieving high line coverage, but almost nothing is actually *verified*. These tests will pass even if every method returns garbage or silently corrupts data.

---

### 🔴 Critical

#### 1. Coverage Touching (Systemic — entire class)

The class methodically calls every public member with no meaningful assertions. 6 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**; the remaining 4 use only `Assert.IsNotNull` which merely checks the return isn't null — never verifying correctness.

---

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE — proves nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER — verify the product was actually stored
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

---

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify the price actually changed
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

---

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify the product is gone
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

---

#### 5. No Assertions — `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify the count is correct
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
```

---

#### 6. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)

This is the most dangerous — `ApplyBulkDiscount` has real arithmetic logic (`Price * (1 - fraction)`) that is never verified.

```csharp
// AFTER — verify prices were actually discounted
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var widget = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, widget!.Price);  // 9.99 * 0.90
```

---

#### 7. No Assertions — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85)

```csharp
// AFTER — verify the imported product exists with correct values
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", imported!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, imported.Price);
